WEBVTT

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.410
Here's your coffee.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.530
Thanks.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.000
Not much longer, right?

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.670
Yep. The train leaves at 4.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.270
It's been a long time since I've taken the train.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.420
This coffee really hits the spot.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.250
And the cold makes it taste even better.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:43.100
This train is leaving East Makinata,
heading for Kanokan! Heading for Kanokan!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.020
We will be boarding passengers shortly!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:54.020
Passengers who already have tickets,
please present them when boarding the train!

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.400
Do you think we can snag some good seats if we board right now?

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.780
These tickets are for reserved seats.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.450
I hope we can get to Lake Kanokan
just as the sun is rising.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.040
Did we really need to leave this early, though?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.290
'Course we did!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.130
Nothing beats fishing in the morning!

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.590
They say Lake Kanokan's a great place to fish.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.760
Plus, I wanted to try riding the night train!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.640
Well... I guess I can understand that.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.140
Do you two have tickets?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.100
Yeah.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.650
Ready to go?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.780
Here. This is for two.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.910
Seats I-2 and 3. Thank you.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.620
Um, I think it's around here...

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.330
Shall I stow it for you?
Um, I think it's around here...

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:54.830
This too, please.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.590
Row S is in the other car.
This too, please.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.920
Oh, it is?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.840
Yeah, I want to wear a scarf when I'm there.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:00.470
Get this too, please.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.260
Mommy, can I have some tea?
Get this too, please.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.890
I told you, we're about to leave.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.350
Here they are.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.600
I-2 and 3...

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.650
Oh, are your seats separated?

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.070
Oh, a conductor.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.830
Mii-chan! Is seat I-1 open?

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.580
Seat I-1?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.080
Let me see...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.920
That one's empty for today.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.750
Okay, thanks!

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.000
You can sit in seats 1 and 2.
I'll just swap out your ticket.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.760
Are you sure?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.050
Thanks a bunch.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.090
Where did you buy those tickets?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.510
A ticket booth in Makinata called Shimaya.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.810
Shimaya, was it? I'll remember that.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.020
Okay...

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.690
I guess it all worked out...

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.530
I wonder if Shimaya's gonna get an earful.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:07.200
Heading to Kanokan! Heading to Kanokan!
We'll be departing shortly!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.380
We started moving!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.300
Yeah.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.970
Hard to tell since it's pitch black outside, though.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.940
Well, how about we grab some breakfast?

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.060
Good idea.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.360
Whoops.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.820
Are you okay?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.830
What are you going to order, Hakumei?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.840
The minced meat bento or fried tofu sushi bento, I think...

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.430
I'm waffling between the cucumber sandwiches and soup.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.350
Seriously? You're not gonna get a bento?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.520
I'm not allowed to eat cucumber sandwiches?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.560
I mean, we're on a train and all.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.100
Excuse me, ladies...

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.690
If you haven't decided, may I go ahead of you?

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.610
Go on ahead!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.740
Beer and deep fried yams.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:30.700
Coming right up.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.710
The fried tofu sushi, cucumber sandwiches, a bowl of soup, and...

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.340
deep fried yams!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.260
Right away!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.890
I'll trade you one of these.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:55.770
Sure!

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.770
Did you see something?

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.360
Yeah. I caught a glimpse of the river.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.380
I wonder where we are right now.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:25.750
No idea.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.300
Wanna open the window and look?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.590
Good idea.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.300
It's stuck...

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.310
That feels nice.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.230
Yeah.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.110
I still have no idea where we are, though.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.860
We're not far from Meisashi.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.240
Oh... Thank you.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.700
Mii-chan!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.950
We'll be making a stop at the Kazashi station in about an hour.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.370
I see.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.040
Back in the old days, this line used to stop at Yakutsu Mine,

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.840
but there's fewer people who want to go there nowadays.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.170
Really?

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:13.590
So now we pass through Hikoto Province,
which has some incredible scenery!

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.850
On the way home, definitely take the Hakufutsu route!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.180
Oh! Would you like to see the route map?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:24.770
You were in the middle of eating, weren't you?
My apologies for rambling on!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.810
It's okay.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.480
Mii-chan sure is something.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:31.900
Yeah.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.630
Morning. You're open for business this early?

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.140
'Course I am. Want to buy something?

00:08:56.430 --> 00:09:00.890
I'll take some ginger tempura and two bottles of orb tea.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.640
You're still eating?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.020
Each stop on the journey hits the reset button on my stomach.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.150
Here you go.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.570
What is this "orb tea"?

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.910
It's a cold-brewed tea. You can only get it in Kazashi.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:24.330
They put water and fresh leaves in a orb-shaped bottle, and it stays sealed up until you drink it.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.170
The leaves themselves aren't anything special, though.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.920
But we're here, so we might as well buy it... right?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.760
When we get home, I'll try to make it with some different leaves.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.180
The ginger tempura is so hot!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.590
Here. That's what the tea's for.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.050
Thanks.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.520
It's got such a pretty color.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.680
Maybe because they're fresh leaves.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.780
The sky's getting lighter.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.740
Yep.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.030
It's about time.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.410
Yeah.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.200
The other stalls have started opening up.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.460
Th-They even sell cloth out here!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.000
We can drop by on the way back.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.840
But they're selling cloth!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.460
But the train is leaving.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.890
We'll be entering the tunnel shortly!
Please close the windows!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.360
Back in the dark, huh?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.950
That's no fun.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.910
I'm here to light the lamps.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.580
Excuse me.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.630
All done. Would you like some coffee or tea?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.170
I'd love some coffee.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.720
Same for me.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.850
This coffee isn't the greatest, huh?

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.360
Mikochi, I'm going to the restroom...

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.890
One more coffee, please.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.140
Coming right up.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.000
Rise and shine, Mikochi.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.880
I had a strange dream...

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.300
You were reading a book.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.010
Oh, we're out of the tunnel.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.800
Not long until we're there.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.140
Rain?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.690
It suddenly started raining.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.820
I see...

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.190
I wonder if it's okay to open the window.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.320
Don't see why not. Lemme put away my bag.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.330
Whoa! It's cold!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.670
I guess rain's okay if you're sitting in a train.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.050
Yeah, I guess it is.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.880
It's too bad that we can't fish, though.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.590
Huh?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.680
Who said we weren't fishing?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.890
This weather's perfect for it.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.270
I brought the raincoats, too.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.100
Oh... I see...

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.520
Fishing in the rain...

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.070
I can't wait to see what we'll catch!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:26.240
We're approaching Kanokan! Last stop!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:33.250
I kind of wish I could stay on the train a little longer...

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.310
Nothing's biting, huh?

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.230
Nothing at all.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:15.000
Just as I expected from Lake Kanokan.
This will require some creative thinking!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.710
I think it's been about three hours since we started, right?

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.500
Something like that, I guess.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:26.130
It's getting kinda chilly out, so d'you wanna head back to the fishing shack for a bit?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.340
G-Great idea!

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.430
The water's nice and cloudy today!

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.890
The big ones will probably show up this evening.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.100
Oh?

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:44.400
<i>Hakumei looks like she's having fun.</i>

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.240
<i>The rain doesn't seem like it's letting up at all.</i>

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:50.910
<i>I want to get back to the inn as soon as possible.</i>

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.040
Nice and warm...

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.120
Don't catch fire.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:07.010
I made that rainwear out of regular cloth,
so it's not that great at keeping us dry.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:07.880
Yeah.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:15.720
Rainwear is usually made of oiled paper,
but you always seem to tear it, Hakumei.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.140
Yeah...

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.440
Are the fish biting today, young ladies?

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.150
Oh, you're the fried yam guy.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.150
The heck are you talking about?

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:32.200
Anyhow, they're not biting at all. No luck here.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.490
Is that right?

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:38.790
It's true that today's been rough. My bones are starting to creak from walking around.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.160
Did you catch anything?

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.210
I caught myself three tiny fish.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.670
No big ones yet.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:49.720
Ah...

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.930
I think I'm just going to sit here for a spell.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.470
What did you use to catch your fish?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.100
Tenkara.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.430
Wow, you're doing tenkara in this rain?

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.770
I was on the bank with all those camellias overhead.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:06.020
Drop the fly in over there, and you'll be set.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.440
I wonder if there's any tackle for rent here.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.530
Red is good. Get a red feather lure.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:17.330
Excuse me, but what is "tenkara"?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.040
Hm? It's fishing with a feather lure.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.460
You don't really go fishing, do you, Miss?

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.840
No, not really...

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:35.760
Then Lake Kanokan might be a tough one for you. It's huge, and the fish are finicky.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:39.890
Yeah, that's so true. We weren't able to catch anything all day!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:44.650
Finished already? The day is still young, you know.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.270
Oh, right. Of course...

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:49.270
They had feather lures!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.820
They're all so pretty.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:53.950
Sure are!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.280
Is this feather from a bird?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.370
Yeah. I think that one's duck.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.330
These are really well-made.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:06.290
I didn't think they'd have such high-quality rental gear.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.250
Let's go try them out!

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.800
Already?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.090
You don't stay in one place when you're doing tenkara.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.680
We need to get out there before the footing gets bad.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.680
We're going to have to walk around, huh?

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.940
I'll go grab the tackle.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.610
Okay. I'll be right behind you.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.070
Miss?

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.190
Yes?

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:39.200
Because we're experienced anglers, we can enjoy our time out here even if we leave empty-handed.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.450
Don't force yourself to do something you won't enjoy.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:47.670
I think Mikochi would be able to handle this one.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.790
I'm not forcing myself...

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.390
It's just a drizzle now.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:01.760
Let's head to the place with the camellias first.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.970
Okay.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:07.600
After that, I want to try to go to the stone steps and the lakehead!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.900
Oh, there it is!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.940
The bank looks treacherous.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:16.990
Yep!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:34.340
Since the lure is so light, there's a trick to casting it.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:40.260
Using the weight of the woven line,
bend it like a whip.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.260
Make it flex overhead,

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:45.770
and then throw it in upstream where you think the fish are.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:51.770
Then, just let the lure drift along, and when the fish come up, take it in real quick.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:56.030
If you feel tension on the line, then you secure the rod to the ground using this hook...

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.030
Right...

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:03.830
Listening to me babble probably won't
help anything. Why don't you try casting it?

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.950
O-Okay.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.260
First catch of the day!

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.550
Don't you mean first flower of the day?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.310
Aw, the line is tangled.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.350
Let's untangle it together.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.060
Sorry.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:34.480
I really like camellias. They look so dignified.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.110
I like them too.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:47.370
Hakumei, I'll do this. You can go ahead and fish.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.080
It's okay. We're nearly done.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:51.290
Okay...

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:06.470
I think using the bobber suits me better.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.640
Yeah?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:18.570
Hey, Hakumei.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.730
Yes?

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:25.660
Fishing is... just boring to me.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:29.910
I thought so.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:31.410
Sorry.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.540
I couldn't keep it in.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.710
I'm a bit annoyed that I can't get into it, actually.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.300
I see...

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.300
It's kind of a shame.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.390
Thinking of all the advice you gave me, too... It makes me feel awful.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.180
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:54.850
Okay then, I'm heading back to the shack now.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.100
You go ahead and—

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.240
Mikochi, the bobber!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.280
Huh?! What?!

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.720
You almost had him, huh?

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:28.430
Yeah.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.970
Wanna head back?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.390
Yeah.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:49.410
Oh, it's you, young ladies. You came at just the right time!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.950
I caught this a moment ago.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.000
What a fish, eh?

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.040
It put up quite the fight!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:03.420
I thought I might die! It came rushing in from around where you ladies were.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:06.840
Hakumei.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:12.100
Will you... teach me to fish again?

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.560
Yeah, I'd be glad to.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:20.190
But next time, let's go to a spot in Makinata... for beginners.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:35.370
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:43.170
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:47.170
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:51.140
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:55.680
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.680 --> 00:23:00.060
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.650
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:07.400
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:11.320
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:16.160
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:20.120
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:24.090
